# Tools the release job uses to build the wheel and sdist. setuptools is the
# build backend and runs under `python -m build --no-isolation`, so the
# hash-pinned version below is exactly what builds the release. It must
# satisfy the range in pyproject.toml [build-system] requires.
#
# twine runs `twine check --strict` on the built files before they are uploaded.
#
# Regenerate for the release job's platform (Linux, Python 3.12). The job
# installs with --no-deps, so the lock must hold the full Linux closure;
# resolving on macOS would drop Linux-only dependencies:
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 \
#     --python-platform x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu --exclude-newer <date 2+ weeks ago> \
#     --output-file .github/build-requirements.txt .github/build-requirements.in
build
setuptools
twine
